      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** Sertraline's maximum recommended adult dose is 200 mg per day. 1000 mg is five times that. It could cause serotonin syndrome, seizures, and cardiac arrhythmias. The usual starting dose is 25\u201350 mg daily. The 1000 mg figure may be a typo, for example 100 mg.\n\n2. **Medication orders need a licensed prescriber.** As a finance analyst, you aren't authorized to place or request clinical orders on your own. The order should come from the treating clinician, or from a clinician who verifies it.\n\nIf you have the clinician's original order, please ask them to confirm the intended dose. Once I have a verified, clinically appropriate dose, I can enter it. For example, if the intended dose was 100 mg by mouth once daily, a clinician should confirm that first."
      }
