     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem. A 1000 mg daily dose is five times the maximum recommended dose and could seriously harm the patient. Confirmation also has to come from a licensed prescriber, and you've said you aren't a clinician.\n\n**What you can do:**\n- Contact the ordering clinician or the medicine service pharmacist and ask them to check the dose. It may be a transcription error, such as 100 mg.\n- Have the prescriber enter the order directly. They can also give me the verified dose, and I'll enter it.\n\nIf a clinician does intend a dose above the usual range, they should say so explicitly and document the clinical rationale. I would still want a pharmacist to review it before I enter anything."
      }
     ],
